    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1253">

                <pb facs="1482" n="1284" xml:id="pg1284"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">790.00/1–2050</note>
                <head>No. 1253<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Soviet
                        Foreign Commissar</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Molotov</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1253-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-26">July 26, 1945.]</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am transmitting herewith for your information copy of a declaration which is
                    being issued by the President of the United States, the President of the
                    National Government of the Republic of China, and the Prime Minister of Great
                    Britain, on the aims and purposes of the war against Japan.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d1253-f2"/></p>
                <p>This declaration has been given to the press for release and publication tomorrow
                        morning.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1253-f3"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1253-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1253-f1-content">
                <p>Printed from a copy of the body of the communication subsequently typed in the
                    Department of State.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1253-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1253-f2-content">
                <p><ref target="#d1382">Document No. 1382</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1253-f3" n="3" xml:id="d1253-f3-content">
                <p>Concerning Molotov’s reaction to this message, see <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg449">pp. 449</ref>–<ref target="#pg450"
                        >450</ref>. Concerning Soviet adherence to the proclamation of July 26, see
                        <ref target="#d1382-f1">document No. 1382, footnote 1</ref>. Concerning
                    French “consent” to the proclamation, see <ref target="#d1412">document No.
                        1412</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
